+
+## Optional source read index
+
+`indexedReading: true` enables optional `readPage` and `prepareReadIndex` capabilities. The default is disabled. A derived SQLite sidecar stores original event coordinates, physical row/frame offsets and native validation metadata; it does not duplicate transcript bodies. Preparing a previously unindexed archive scans it once in a cancellable source worker. Subsequent append-only updates validate the new suffix, and page reads decode selected original rows or Zstandard frames plus their complete native dependencies. Source replacement, truncation or a same-size revision rebuilds the index. No committed generation, write lease or execution owner changes.
+
+A compressed frame is indivisible. An old single-frame archive can require that complete frame to be decoded even for a small logical page. Index preparation is not evidence of browser responsiveness or production acceptance.
