new file mode 100644
index 00000000..7fc3443d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/ext/upstream-pr/0008.md
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Upstream PR draft: optional source-side native Session page reads
+
+A read-only remote client currently opens and decodes the complete JSONL Session before selecting its first page. Large logs consequently delay the first usable conversation even when only a bounded tail is required.
+
+Add optional `SessionPersistence.readPage` and `prepareReadIndex` capabilities. The JSONL provider enables them with `indexedReading: true`, streams native coordinates and physical offsets into a derived SQLite index, and returns original events with their dependency closure. Native sequence identity, append ownership and durable generations remain unchanged. A fixed observed prefix permits ongoing native append; cancellation leaves the previous SQLite transaction available. Complete-result admission can reduce a body page while retaining all dependencies, and reports an explicit capacity error if one atomic item cannot fit.
+
+Reuse a checkpointable V4 lifecycle validator for both complete restoration and indexed suffix validation. Preserve open tool, compaction, inheritance, delivery, title and request-header rules. Index preparation remains an explicit source-side scan for preexisting archives. Warm IO is bounded by selected source rows or Zstandard frames, and an indivisible historical frame can exceed the logical page's physical cost.
+
+Tests use actual source files and isolated workers and compare retained native lifecycles across checkpoints. They cover dependency closure, append-only suffix validation, quota admission, torn physical tails, unknown required vocabulary and cancellation. The extension is disabled by default. This draft has not been submitted upstream.
